    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on July 23, 2026, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** anchors the lineup with the day\u2019s highest efficiency score of 67.11. Despite facing a standard right-hander in Legumina, his projection benefits from a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole, offering the most stable floor for production. While **Drake Baldwin** registers a 59.15, he remains a high-upside play; batting leadoff against Hart provides a significant boost, and his solid xwOBA of 0.387 suggests he is well-positioned to capitalize on his premium lineup placement. We are sacrificing efficiency with **Brayan Rocchio** (44.53) and **Dominic Smith** (40.68) today, as both are navigating middling matchups; **Dominic Smith** in particular faces a steep Platoon disadvantage, though he stays in the mix due to a lack of elite alternatives on the bench.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our depth pieces, with **Jackson Merrill** falling just short of a start. While his base projection was competitive, the combination of a tough matchup against Sale and his projected lower-order placement pushed him below our replacement threshold, prioritizing the consistency of our top four. We are also mindful of the risk surrounding **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**, as the matchup against Hart is currently pending final official confirmation; should the lineup order shift, we may see further volatility in their efficiency scores. With heavy hitters like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** currently on an off-day, the Waves are relying on this core group to maintain our standing in the competitive 5x5 Roto landscape.",
